./logs/iter_002_ideas.stderr.log:641:## Rare bad histories can break essential sup without large average loss
./logs/iter_002_ideas.stderr.log:643:Facts needed: Essential supremum over histories can keep \(\beta(H)\) large, while \(\Delta_T(H)/T\) remains small because the histories almost never occur.
./logs/iter_002_ideas.stderr.log:644:Why it matters: Would show strict weakness of average truncation criteria compared with \(\beta\).
./logs/iter_002_ideas.stderr.log:648:## Tiny-price long-delay blocks may break raw beta without meaningful regret
./logs/iter_002_ideas.stderr.log:650:Facts needed: For every \(h\), some block creates a conditional state with \(\Pr(h<\tau<\infty)=1\), so \(\beta(h)=1\). But if \(p_m\) decreases fast enough, total best fixed comparator value may be \(o(T)\), making sublinear regret trivial.
./logs/iter_002_ideas.stderr.log:657:Facts: Then counterfactual rewards \(r_t^H(b)\) for unplayed grid quotes may not be determined by the realized future price path, or may correspond to a different path under a comparator policy.
./logs/iter_002_ideas.stderr.log:666:Attempt: Prove that sublinear regret is possible only if the essential-sup hitting tail \(\beta(h)\to0\).
./logs/iter_002_ideas.stderr.log:667:Failure: False under law-aware/process-wise quantifiers. For iid uniform prices, \(\beta(h)=1\) for all \(h\), but a learner knowing the law can play the best fixed quote in expectation and get zero regret.
./logs/iter_002_ideas.stderr.log:673:Failure: Singleton terminal-spike law has zero law-aware regret but \(\Delta_T(H)=\Omega(T)\) for \(H=o(T)\).
./logs/iter_002_ideas.stderr.log:678:Attempt: View \((r_t^H(b))_{b\in\mathcal G_K}\) as a delayed full-information reward vector in the original market protocol.
./logs/iter_002_ideas.stderr.log:685:Failure: Regret compares to \(\sup_a\mathbb E\sum_t r_t(a)\). With iid block types, the best fixed expected comparator can be the same Bayes action available to the learner, so per-block realized optimal-action gaps do not add.
./logs/iter_002_ideas.stderr.log:691:Failure: For fixed \(D\), delay is bounded by \(D\), so asymptotic regret is \(O(D)=o(T)\) and \(\beta(h)=0\) for \(h\ge D\).
